{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md && cat docs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md'","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL project instructions\n\n## Mission entry point\n\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\n\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\n\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\n\n## Working rules\n\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\n- Follow the applicable policies under\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\n\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\n# Bounded reconstruction v1\n\nThis executable profile addresses MC08–MC12, MC18 and MC26. It constructs a joint\nfamily from declared templates, slots, openings, dated mappings and admitted\nobservations. It does not discover templates or infer arbitrary company histories.\n\n## Pre-execution research intent and evidence contract\n\nQuestion: do declared inputs generate the correct family within their finite\nscope? Mechanism: rational linear constraints with shared economic identifiers,\nexplicit finite choices and bounded integer domains. Expected failure modes are\nlost dependence, wrong strict endpoints, unexamined rounding and false completeness.\nComparators are an independent Fraction replay/enumerator over original fixtures\nand analytic continuous bounds. Exact feasible-set equality and endpoint proofs\nare pass criteria. Unsupported operations, unknown backend replies, unfinished\ncells or unresolved matching obligations veto exact certification. Corrupted\ninputs or protection failures veto acceptance and stop the checker. A numerical\nfailure triggers repair, not rejection of the research direction. Runtime is\nexplanatory only. No superiority, general accounting validity, forecast validity,\ncontinuous probabilistic inference or human acceptance follows from these checks.\nConformance JSON and result.md preserve results; progress.md is a reset checkpoint.\n\nSkeptical audit: the earlier ambiguity between named views and search choices is\nresolved explicitly below. Baselines use original inputs, not generated expected\nanswers. Fixture sizes and budgets are engineering choices. No stochastic ranking\nor production-default promotion is attempted. A successful command can still be\nmisleading if both construction and oracle share lowering; the oracle therefore\nreplays postings independently. The integration checks inspect the unnamed\ninterior, not only endpoint extrema.\n\n## Assumptions and defaults\n\n| Choice | Provenance/status | Justification | Failure mode / early diagnostic |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fraction arithmetic | Core contract, reviewed requirement | exact disclosed decimals | binary-float drift; reject floats |\n| Z3 rational linear solving | existing 4.16.0, implementation hypothesis | exact linear SAT and optimisation | shared backend error; independent enumeration and algebra |\n| finite templates/slots | explicit input, scope hypothesis | tractable reconstruction | omitted histories; preserve exclusions and obligations |\n| budgets | explicit caller input, convenience | bounded execution | premature stop; zero-work and one-cell tests |\n| rounding convention/stage | explicit input, no inferred default | preserve disclosure versus posting semantics | wrong ties; negative/parity fixtures |\n| finite probability measure | explicit joint atoms, hypothesis | dependence and exact Bayes update | overlap/double use; reject duplicate atoms/information |\n| grouping | explicit additive debt profile only | retain contract memory | different resets/maturities/horizon; revalidation tests |\n| deterministic fixtures | engineering comparator | exhaustive small checks | not representative; no empirical forecast claim |\n\n## Family and query semantics\n\nParent P contains opening, slot, transition, mapping and observation constraints.\nNamed view i supplies A_i only. A parent query uses P; a single-view query uses\nP AND A_i. Multiple views require explicit intersection or union. Views may\noverlap or fail to cover P; labels supply neither exclusivity nor probabilities.\nActual finite choices enumerate all declared values jointly. Boolean predicates\nare split by an exhaustive truth-assignment partition of their atomic comparisons;\neach cell includes the formula and its decision prefix. The partition is disjoint\nby construction. Integer variables are enumerated only with finite declared bounds.\nEach candidate assignment/predicate cell is counted once, including infeasible\ncells. Views do not add cells unless their explicit Boolean predicate requires a\nlogical partition. Continuous regions remain symbolic. Unvisited suffixes are\nrepresented by ordinal range and the unchanged family formula.\n\nSlots instantiate nonnegative amounts and an active flag; inactive means zero.\nActive zero is permitted. Both signed posting incidence and economic-state\ncoefficients are declared by the template. Exact context equality is required\nfor observations. One observation ID cannot silently supply incompatible domains.\nUnmatched obligations remain unresolved. Admission records keep six uncertainty\ncategories separate. Stress is conditional, not observed evidence or a likelihood.\n\n## Numerical semantics\n\nFeasibility is checked on each original strict cell before closure optimisation.\nA nonempty convex linear cell has the same infimum/supremum as its closure: for\nany original feasible point x and any closure point y, (1-t)y+t x satisfies every\nstrict inequality for 0<t<=1 and tends to y. The solver therefore optimises closed\ninequalities, proves no better closed value, then tests equality with the endpoint\nunder original constraints. Empty strict cells never acquire relaxation witnesses.\nUnknown in any proof or endpoint test leaves the bound uncertified. Unbounded,\nUnknown, Infeasible and PartialSearch remain distinct. Partial-cell extrema are\nexplored-only, never global certificates.\n\nDebt amounts F,V satisfy F>=0, V>=0, F+V=D. For exact D>0, alpha=F/D is equivalent\nto the fraction parameterisation. With rounded D, use amounts directly. A fixed\nfraction comparison F/D op a may multiply by D only after proving D>0 (or reverse\nthe comparison after proving D<0). Unknown sign or an unknown threshold is\nunsupported. Unknown-by-unknown products and unbounded integer domains are also\nunsupported; they never imply infeasibility.\n\nDisclosure intervals retain inclusion flags. Half-even display domains include\nboth ties for an even displayed minor-unit integer and neither for an odd one.\nPosting quantisation rounds exact rationals at the declared boundary. Symbolic\nposting amounts use bounded integers; continuous relaxation is forbidden.\n\nFinite measures use unique joint atom IDs with weights summing to one. Conditional\nviews are events on atoms. Likelihood information blocks can be used once. Default\nand unresolved mass are retained; unavailable outcomes prevent an unconditional\nmean. Grouping requires matching rate/reset/maturity/hedge keys and additive\ntransition/report checks for the explicit scenario and horizon; contract memory\nis retained. These tests do not prove general aggregation equivalence.\n\n## Execution\n\nUse existing Python/Z3, standard library and accepted P03 dependencies; install\nnothing. Run `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p04.py' -v`\nand the analogous P03 regression, followed by `python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p04.py\n--output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04 --execution-inventory\n data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/phase-entry-inventory.json`.\nNo accelerator framework is used; CPU-only checks intentionally hide GPU devices.\nThe checker records actual versions, elapsed time, hashes, generated formulas,\nproof queries, observations and protection comparisons. Git is unavailable; content\nhashes preserve provenance. Human acceptance remains pending.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
