{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,45p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py && sed -n '229,249p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Executed P03 obligations; authored typed inputs never pass through the parser.\"\"\"\nimport copy\nfrom dataclasses import replace\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'scripts'))\nimport core0_ir_v1 as ir\nfrom core0_frontends_v1 import compile_source\nimport jsonschema\n\nOBSERVATIONS = []\nBASE = (ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc').read_text()\nREASON = 'Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed'\nRENAMED = '''module FinancingStudy version \"2\";\nuse DemoDebt version \"1\";\nsource disclosure = external(\"synthetic-note-7\");\nentity Beta functional USD;\nbook Statutory entity Beta basis DemoDebt version \"1\";\naccount Cash : Asset book Statutory;\naccount Debt : Liability book Statutory;\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Statutory;\naccount Retained : Equity book Statutory;\nopening carried for Statutory from external(\"after-2025-close\");\nobservation borrowing : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 150 USD from disclosure;\nsymbol share : Real in [0, 1] because \"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\";\ncontract facility : DebtMix book Statutory {\n principal = value(borrowing); fixed_fraction = share;\n fixed_rate = 0.05 per year; initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\n}\nalternative fixed { assume share == 1; }\nalternative floating { assume share == 0; }\nscenario shock { set market_rate = constant(0.08 per year); }\nreport financials for Statutory { mapping = external(\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\"); }\n'''\n\n\ndef bindings(principal=100, renamed=False):\nUncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\nMeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\ndomain, evidence, dependencies and admission rule. An election needs a dated\npermitted treatment and evidence of eligibility; a balanced but prohibited\ntreatment is UnsupportedTreatment. Estimates need a method/date/inputs; future\ninnovations need a joint law and measure. New observations constrain facts;\ncorrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\nhypothetical stresses alone do none of those.\n\nExogenousStress supplies named driver paths without updating historical weights.\nObservationalConditioning supplies observed events, a joint model and positive\nevent probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\nweights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\nweights. Continuous density conditioning requires an explicit conditional\nmodel/regular conditional distribution adapter. StructuralIntervention replaces\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\nand real-world simulation measures have different IDs and cannot be mixed\nwithout an explicit justified transformation.\n\nInformationView(date, observer, role, evidence_view, committed_prefix,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
